# Pulseboard Monolith Overview

Local-first analytics platform. Work from the repository root.

The running code is the hello entry in `apps/pulseboard-server`. Packages below are the target layout. Do not describe them as live until the code exists.

## Read first

1. `docs/engineering/project-plan.md`
2. `docs/engineering/README.md`
3. `docs/engineering/how-we-work/feature-placement.md`
4. `AGENTS.md`

## Target repo map

```
apps/pulseboard-server/          → thin FastAPI shell
apps/pulseboard-worker/          → aggregate + anomaly worker (no LLM)

packages/module-events/          → event ingest
packages/module-metrics/         → aggregates, funnels, segments
packages/module-anomalies/       → spike/drop, alerts, incident reports
packages/module-chat/            → threads + SSE
packages/module-ai/              → LangGraph agents via AiModule only

libs/pulseboard-core/            → ports (LlmPort and read ports)
libs/pulseboard-models/          → ORM only
libs/pulseboard-connectors/      → Postgres, Redis, Ollama

mcp/                             → our MCP server; tools call facades
```

Live today: the thin hello shell. Planned: FastAPI in that shell, and the packages above. Vector search is not part of v1.

## Golden rules

1. Thin app shell — no domain logic in `apps/*/main.py`.
2. One module = one domain.
3. Cross-module calls only via `module_*/api.py`.
4. ORM only in `pulseboard-models`.
5. Production agents are compiled LangGraph graphs invoked from the API through `AiModule`.
6. The agent reads tool aggregates. It does not receive raw event dumps.
7. Ollama is the LLM adapter. The app runs without the model.
8. Our MCP server is the tool surface. A third-party MCP server is not the core.

